{
  "id": "fluency-l3-opening-brackets",
  "course": "equations",
  "lesson": "l3-opening-brackets",
  "title": "Fluency: opening brackets",
  "sample": true,
  "n": 20,
  "pass": 0.9,
  "minutes": 10,
  "families": [
    {
      "id": "expand-single",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "expand a single bracket",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [2, 9] },
        "b": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] },
        "v": { "pick": ["x", "y", "t"] }
      },
      "let": { "p": "a*b" },
      "prompt": "Expand ${a}({v}{b:+})$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{a}{v}{p:+}", "form": "expanded" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "first-term-only", "tex": "{a}{v}{b:+}", "line": "You multiplied only the first term by {a}." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "${a} \\times {v} = {a}{v}$ and ${a} \\times {b:()} = {p}$.",
        "So ${a}({v}{b:+}) = {a}{v}{p:+}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "factorise-common",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "factorise by a common factor",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [2, 9] },
        "b": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] },
        "v": { "pick": ["x", "y", "t"] }
      },
      "let": { "p": "a*b" },
      "prompt": "Factorise ${a}{v}{p:+}$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{a}({v}{b:+})", "form": "factorised" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "constant-unchanged", "tex": "{a}({v}{p:+})", "line": "You took {a} out of the first term but left {p:()} as it was." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Both terms share the factor {a}: ${a}{v} = {a} \\times {v}$ and ${p} = {a} \\times {b:()}$.",
        "So ${a}{v}{p:+} = {a}({v}{b:+})$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "antiderivative-power",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "integrate a power",
      "vars": {
        "k": { "int": [2, 9] },
        "m": { "int": [1, 9] }
      },
      "let": { "c": "m*(k+1)", "k1": "k+1" },
      "prompt": "Find an antiderivative of ${c}x^{{{k}}}$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{m:c}x^{{{k1}}}", "upToConstant": true },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "power-not-raised", "tex": "{c}x^{{{k1}}}", "line": "You raised the power but did not divide by {k1}." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Raise the power to {k1} and divide by {k1}: ${c}x^{{{k1}}} \\div {k1} = {m:c}x^{{{k1}}}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluate-linear",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "substitute into a linear expression",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [2, 9] },
        "b": { "int": [-6, 6], "not": [0] },
        "x": { "int": [-5, 5], "not": [0, 1] }
      },
      "let": { "r": "a + b*x" },
      "where": ["a + b*x != (a + b)*x", "a + b*x != a - b*x"],
      "prompt": "Work out ${a}{b:+c}x$ when $x = {x}$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{r}", "tol": { "abs": 0 } },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "added-first", "value": "{(a + b)*x}", "line": "Multiply {b:()} by {x:()} before you add {a}." },
        { "id": "sign-slip", "value": "{a - b*x}", "line": "Check the sign of the second term." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "${b:()} \\times {x:()} = {b*x}$.",
        "${a} + {b*x:()} = {r}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "add-fractions",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "add two fractions",
      "vars": {
        "p": { "int": [1, 5] },
        "q": { "int": [2, 7] },
        "r": { "int": [1, 5] },
        "s": { "int": [2, 7] }
      },
      "let": { "total": "p/q + r/s" },
      "where": ["q != s", "p < q", "r < s", "total != (p + r)/(q + s)"],
      "prompt": "Work out $\\frac{{{p}}}{{{q}}} + \\frac{{{r}}}{{{s}}}$. Give a fraction or a decimal.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{total}", "tol": { "abs": 0.0005 }, "accept": "${total:frac}$, or a decimal within 0.0005" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "added-tops-and-bottoms", "value": "{(p + r)/(q + s)}", "tol": { "abs": 0.0005 }, "line": "Do not add the tops and the bottoms: give both fractions the same bottom first." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "A common bottom is ${q*s}$: $\\frac{{{p*s}}}{{{q*s}}} + \\frac{{{r*q}}}{{{q*s}}}$.",
        "That is ${total:frac}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "factorise-fully",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "factorise fully",
      "vars": { "k": { "int": [2, 5] }, "p": { "int": [-6, 6], "not": [0] }, "q": { "int": [-6, 6], "not": [0] }, "v": { "pick": ["x", "y", "t"] } },
      "where": ["p < q", "p + q != 0"],
      "prompt": "Factorise fully ${poly(v; k, k*(p+q), k*p*q)}$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{k}({v}{p:+})({v}{q:+})", "form": "factorised-fully" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "common-factor-dropped", "tex": "({v}{p:+})({v}{q:+})", "line": "You left out the common factor ${k}$." },
        { "id": "signs-swapped", "tex": "{k}({v}{-p:+})({v}{-q:+})", "line": "Check the signs: the numbers in the brackets add to ${p+q}$ and multiply to ${p*q}$." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Take out {k} first: ${poly(v; k, k*(p+q), k*p*q)} = {k}({poly(v; 1, p+q, p*q)})$.",
        "Then ${poly(v; 1, p+q, p*q)} = ({v}{p:+})({v}{q:+})$, because ${p} + {q:()} = {p+q}$ and ${p} \\times {q:()} = {p*q}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "complete-the-square",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "complete the square",
      "vars": { "a": { "int": [1, 3] }, "h": { "int": [-6, 6], "not": [0] }, "q": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] }, "v": { "pick": ["x", "y", "t"] } },
      "where": ["a*(h*h + q) != q"],
      "prompt": "Write ${poly(v; a, 2*a*h, a*(h*h+q))}$ as a bracket squared plus a number.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{a:c}({v}{h:+})^2{q:+}", "form": "completed-square" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "constant-not-adjusted", "tex": "{a:c}({v}{h:+})^2{a*(h*h+q):+}", "line": "The bracket already supplies ${a*h*h}$, so the number added must be ${q}$." },
        { "id": "sign-in-bracket", "tex": "{a:c}({v}{-h:+})^2{q:+}", "line": "The number in the bracket has the same sign as the middle term." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "The bracket ${a:c}({v}{h:+})^2$ expands to ${poly(v; a, 2*a*h, a*h*h)}$.",
        "The constant needs ${q}$ more, so ${poly(v; a, 2*a*h, a*(h*h+q))} = {a:c}({v}{h:+})^2{q:+}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "roots-numeric",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "solve a quadratic for both roots",
      "vars": { "roots": { "pick": [[-7, -3], [-7, -2], [-7, 2], [-7, 4], [-6, -4], [-6, 4], [-5, -3], [-5, -1], [-5, 1], [-5, 2], [-5, 4], [-4, -3], [-4, -1], [-4, 5], [-4, 7], [-3, 4], [-3, 6], [-2, -1], [-1, 2], [-1, 3], [-1, 5], [-1, 6], [1, 6], [1, 7], [2, 4], [2, 5], [3, 7], [4, 5], [4, 6], [5, 6]], "as": ["r", "s"] }, "v": { "pick": ["x", "y", "t"] } },
      "prompt": "Solve ${poly(v; 1, -(r+s), r*s)} = 0$. Give both values, separated by a comma.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answers": ["{r}", "{s}"], "unordered": true, "tol": { "abs": 0 }, "accept": "${r}$ and ${s}$, in either order" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "signs-flipped", "value": "{-r}, {-s}", "line": "The roots make the brackets zero, so each has the opposite sign to the number in its bracket." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Factorise: ${poly(v; 1, -(r+s), r*s)} = ({v}{-r:+})({v}{-s:+})$.",
        "Each bracket is zero for one root, so ${v} = {r}$ or ${v} = {s}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "roots-expression",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "solve a quadratic with fractional roots",
      "vars": { "ac": { "pick": [[1, 2], [1, 3], [2, 3], [1, 4], [3, 4], [2, 5]], "as": ["a", "c"] }, "b": { "int": [-6, 6], "not": [0] }, "d": { "int": [-6, 6], "not": [0] }, "v": { "pick": ["x", "y", "t"] } },
      "where": ["b*c != a*d", "b*c != -a*d"],
      "prompt": "Solve ${poly(v; a*c, a*d+b*c, b*d)} = 0$. Give both values, separated by a comma.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answers": ["{-b/a:frac}", "{-d/c:frac}"], "unordered": true },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "signs-flipped", "tex": "{b/a:frac}, {d/c:frac}", "line": "Each root has the opposite sign to the number in its bracket." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Factorise: ${poly(v; a*c, a*d+b*c, b*d)} = ({poly(v; a, b)})({poly(v; c, d)})$.",
        "Set each bracket to zero: ${v} = {-b/a:frac}$ or ${v} = {-d/c:frac}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "roots-surd",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "solve a quadratic with surd roots",
      "vars": { "h": { "int": [-5, 5], "not": [0] }, "d": { "pick": [2, 3, 5, 6, 7, 10, 11] }, "v": { "pick": ["x", "y", "t"] } },
      "prompt": "Solve ${poly(v; 1, -2*h, h*h-d)} = 0$. Give the exact roots.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answers": ["{h}+\\sqrt{{{d}}}", "{h}-\\sqrt{{{d}}}"], "unordered": true },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "centre-sign", "tex": "{-h}+\\sqrt{{{d}}}, {-h}-\\sqrt{{{d}}}", "line": "The roots are centred on ${h}$, the opposite sign to the number in the bracket." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Complete the square: ${poly(v; 1, -2*h, h*h-d)} = ({v}{-h:+})^2 - {d}$.",
        "So ${v} = {h} \\pm \\sqrt{{{d}}}$."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
